{"ts":"2026-09-05T18:14:27.716Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"grok-4.6","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"1e64c2203adf74b8d8740a12","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"grok-4.6","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-05T18:14:27.716Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-09-05T18:14:27.716Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"pm-cli 2026.9.5 added a delivery ledger kind. Typecheck failed because buildUsageReport treated every non-touch event as a serve and read event.rows. An unflagged changelog run now emits the bare ## <version> heading; this repo already asserted that the flag changes the heading rather than pinning the clock, so that gate stayed green. Affinity fixtures that wrote legacy serve rows were classified untrusted and scored 0; they now write v2 serve+delivery. Revert-proof: the three new delivery tests failed 3/3 against the old parser (parse returned null, readLedger counted malformed, buildUsageReport threw event.rows is not iterable) and passed 3/3 after the fix. npm run release:check exit 0. pm health --strict-exit exit 0."}]}],"before_hash":"5c02235e022cf854ef6c68e0632c2e14019e9cde78d40448bef5aedb25441184","after_hash":"b564d587583b8163650e0bd1be1235f70761738987ae75224bcb90b0efc174b6","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"12361a0e419f618efd9be427d273d008bd053b8f6c8016c102eaef6b5ec56d7f"}
